<link rel="layout" href="{{layoutHref}}">
<head>
  <title>@data.status · @data.title</title>
</head>
@* The error page: no URL of its own and no `load`, and the same layout as every other page.
   Its `data` is the error that brought the user here: `status`, `title`, `detail` when the
   server said something, `path` (what was asked, without the app's base), `back` (where the
   user came from, when it is of this app) and `home` (the app's home). `back` and `home`
   already carry the app's base: write them as they are in an `href`.
   If the layout asks for props, resolve them in `_error.fudapi` with `layout`: its handler
   gets the same error as `data`. *@
<h1>@data.status · @data.title</h1>
@if (data.detail !== undefined) {
  <p>@data.detail</p>
}
@if (data.back !== undefined) {
  <p><a href=@data.back>Back</a></p>
} @else {
  <p><a href=@data.home>Home</a></p>
}
